    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6027A\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Dr. Robert C. \"Doc\" Schelin Memorial\nHighway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE::\n\nDesignates all that portion of the state highway system constituting\nState Route 340 between Thorpe Drive and State Route 303 in the town of\nOrangetown, County of Rockland, shall be designated and be known as the\n\"Dr. Robert C. \"Doc\" Schelin Memorial Highway.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS::\n\nSection I: Amends the highway law by adding a new section 345-b, which\ndesignates all that portion of the state highway system constituting\nState Route 340 between Thorpe Drive and State Route 303 in the town of\nOrangetown, County of Rockland, shall be designated and be known as the\n\"Dr. Robert C. \"Doc\" Schelin Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection II: States that the commissioner of transportation shall provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway system as designated pursuant to section 1 of this act. The use\nand placement of such signs shall be determined by the local munici-\npality. The designation will be for ceremonial purposes only, and the\nofficial name of the bridge will not be changed as a result of this act.\n\nSection III: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION::\n\nDr. Robert C. \"Doc\" Schelin was a longtime resident of Rockland County\nand pillar of his community. His storied career includes leadership in\neducation, local government, public safety, and serving as Tappan's own\nSanta Claus.\n\nUbiquitously known as \"Doc\", Dr. Schelin was a 50-year life member of\nthe Volunteer Fire Association of Tappan, including serving as President\nand Secretary of Commissioners for the Tappan Fire District. In addition\nto educating future generations at St. Thomas Aquinas College, he served\nas a representative for both the men's and women's basketball teams,\nDean of Student Affairs, and on the Rockland Community College Board of\nTrustees.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY::\n\n2021-2022: A.10055-A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS::\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE::\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
